Core Mechanics of RAG Retrieval:
 The pipeline relies on converting unstructured data into a structured search ecosystem before a query is even executed:

Vector retrieval / similarity measurements:
    ________
   |
   ├── Euclidean distance
   |   Measures the straight-line distance between two vectors in multi-dimensional space. Smaller distance means more similar.
   |
   |   Point A  ●────────────● Point B
   |            straight-line distance
   |
   |              n
   |   d(A,B) = √ Σ (Aᵢ − Bᵢ)²
   |              i=1
   |
   ├── Cosine similarity
   |   Measures how similar the directions of two vectors are, regardless of their length/magnitude.
   |
   |   Similar direction
   |      ↗ A
   |     ↗ B
   |   High cosine similarity
   |   Two vectors can have different lengths but point in nearly the same direction.
   |
   |                  n
   |                  Σ AᵢBᵢ
   |                  i=1
   |   cos(A,B) = ─────────────────
   |               ||A|| × ||B||
   |
   ├── Inner product
   |   Measures similarity by combining both vector direction and vector magnitude. Larger inner product generally means greater similarity.
   |   Unlike cosine similarity, vector length matters.
   |
   |   Inner product:
   |         direction
   |           +
   |         magnitude 
   |     matter.
   |
   |           n
   |   A · B = Σ AᵢBᵢ
   |           i=1
   |
   ├── Hamming distance
   |   Counts how many corresponding bits differ between two binary vectors. Smaller distance means more similar.
   |
   |             n
   |   dH(A,B) = Σ [Aᵢ ≠ Bᵢ]
   |             i=1
   |   where each difference contributes 1.
   |
   └── Jaccard similarity
   |   Measures similarity between two sets by comparing how many items they share with the total number of unique items across both sets.
   |
   |              |A ∩ B|
   |   J(A,B) = ───────────
   |              |A ∪ B|
   |______


